comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-01T15:21:58.266Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: complete all-status searches for jscpd 5.1.0 and the live outdated set found closed compatible refresh pm-vwuidf plus canonical open incompatible-major owners pm-ksr40d and pm-do5b, but no owner for jscpd 5.1.0. Registry metadata declares Node >=18, compatible with pm-cli >=22.18.0; live GitHub alert inventories and pnpm audit are zero."
  "2026-09-01T15:22:46.007Z","harness:codex","Live registry correction: jscpd 5.1.1 became current after the initial 5.1.0 resolution. It retains Node >=18 compatibility and adds a Windows ARM64 optional artifact; the package manager recorded every platform artifact in the strict minimum-release-age exception list. The active item now owns 5.1.1, and pnpm outdated contains only pm-ksr40d/npm-package-arg 14 and pm-do5b/TypeScript 7."
  "2026-09-01T15:48:16.167Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-09-01: package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml resolve jscpd 5.1.1, including the new Windows ARM64 optional artifact in the strict minimum-release-age exception set. Both repository and source duplicate scans report zero clones. Full static quality passed; exact coverage passed 596 files / 8260 tests at 100/100/100/100; the packed artifact passed at 19,484,451 bytes and 1,411 files with no source maps; packed npx and bunx smoke passed across 13 packages; previously completed clean installed npm and Bun sessions passed 11 steps each. pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities across 424 dependencies, and live Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning inventories are each zero. pnpm outdated now contains only npm-package-arg 14 owned by pm-ksr40d and TypeScript 7 owned by pm-do5b, both incompatible-major deferrals verified from current registry peer/runtime contracts."
  "2026-09-01T16:36:06.360Z","harness:codex","Review correction: Cubic identified that recurs_from targeted pm-vwuidf, whose full live record owns Greptile, @types/node, and Sentry refreshes but not jscpd. Full live verification identified pm-87hmdw as the canonical prior jscpd 5.0.15 tooling refresh. Replaced the edge with pm-87hmdw,recurs_from; no duplicate item was created."
  "2026-09-01T17:16:30.396Z","harness:codex","Review round evidence: corrected recurs_from from unrelated pm-vwuidf to canonical prior jscpd owner pm-87hmdw after full live record verification. Latest jscpd 5.1.1 remains installed; linked dual-config duplicate scan passed with 0 clones across 1,157 total files and 456 source files. Full static quality and exact coverage also passed after the review fixes."
  "2026-09-01T23:25:22.795Z","harness:codex","Terminal evidence: linked coverage passed with exact 100/100/100/100 totals (61,009 statements, 46,099 branches, 12,701 functions, 58,725 lines). Linked pnpm quality:static passed in a tracker-seeded sandbox in 430.507s, including ESLint, jscpd zero clones, build and generated-contract checks, repository assurance, SDK/package parity, surface replication (2/2 members, density 1), grammar/refusal/token gates, MCP deprecations, graph composition, and record integrity. Earlier schema-context static attempts correctly failed because an empty synthetic tracker cannot satisfy repository defect-evidence assurance; the first tracker-context retry then exposed the incomplete replication set and led to the paired metadata-index fix before this terminal pass. No real tracker data was exposed to tests."
